{
  "title": "Non ci {ip:credo}: te ne {tp:avevo} già {tp:parlato}",
  "translation": "I don't believe it: I had already told you about it",
  "topics": "Combined pronouns in all positions, the different meanings of ci and ne",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Combined pronouns: where they stand"
      },
      "Before a conjugated verb, they stay separate, except *glie-*, which joins the next pronoun. After an infinitive, a gerund or an informal imperative, they form one word with the verb.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Position",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Before the verb",
              "Te lo {ip:dico}. Glielo {ip:dico}. Ce li {ip:porta}."
            ],
            [
              "After an infinitive",
              "{ip:Voglio} dirtelo. {ip:Devo} portarglieli."
            ],
            [
              "With a modal: both are possible",
              "Te lo {ip:voglio} dire. {ip:Voglio} dirtelo."
            ],
            [
              "After an informal command",
              "{imv:Dammelo}! {imv:Portaglieli}!"
            ],
            [
              "With a formal command",
              "Me lo {imv:dia}! Gliela {imv:porti}!"
            ],
            [
              "Negative command",
              "Non dirmelo! Non me lo dire!"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "In the compound tenses, the participle agrees with *lo, la, li, le*, and with *ne* when it means a quantity: *Gliel'{pp:ho dat**a**}. Ce li {pp:ha portat**i**}. Ne {pp:ho mangiat**e**} due.*",
      {
        "h": "What ci can replace"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "It replaces",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a place",
              "Ci {ip:vado} domani.",
              "there"
            ],
            [
              "a + thing (idea)",
              "Non ci {ip:credo}. (credere a)",
              "in it"
            ],
            [
              "a + thing",
              "Ci {ip:penso} io. (pensare a)",
              "about it"
            ],
            [
              "su + thing",
              "{ip:Puoi} contarci. (contare su)",
              "on it"
            ],
            [
              "con + person or thing",
              "Ci {ip:esco} stasera. (uscire con)",
              "with him / her"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "With people, *ci* is usually avoided: *{ip:Penso} a mia madre → {ip:Penso} a lei*, and verbs like *telefonare a* take *gli* or *le*.",
      {
        "h": "What ne can replace"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "It replaces",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a quantity",
              "Ne {ip:voglio} due.",
              "of them"
            ],
            [
              "di + thing",
              "Ne {pp:abbiamo parlato}. (parlare di)",
              "about it"
            ],
            [
              "da + place",
              "Ne {pp:sono} appena {pp:uscito}. (uscire da)",
              "from there"
            ],
            [
              "di + cause",
              "Ne {ip:sono} contento. (contento di)",
              "about it"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Many verbs and adjectives take *a* or *di*, so that the preposition tells you which pronoun you need: *ricordarsi di → Me ne {ip:ricordo}*, *riuscire a → Ci riesco*."
    ]
  },
